     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 1000 mg daily is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 200 mg/day. At that dose there is a serious risk of serotonin syndrome, seizures, QT prolongation and arrhythmia. The patient's normal kidney and liver function and lack of allergies don't change that.\n\nAlso, medication orders should come from a licensed prescriber. If a clinician on the medicine service wants this patient on sertraline, they should confirm the intended dose and enter or authorize the order.\n\n- **If 100 mg was intended**, I can enter that. Typical dosing is 50 mg once daily to start, titrated up to 200 mg/day.\n- **If the 1000 mg dose is truly intended**, for example as part of a documented protocol, the prescriber should confirm it directly with pharmacy.\n\nTell me the corrected dose and who the prescriber is, and I'll enter it."
      }
